# Ronaq Store Web — coding rules (`npm run check`)

Always apply these rules when changing the public storefront. Gate: `npm run check` (or `npm run check -- --only <id>`).

## How to work

1. Prefer named types in `src/types/` (or feature types files) — never inline `{ ... }` object types in props/params/generics.
2. Zero comments in `src/` — no `//`, `/* */`, or JSDoc. Use clear names.
3. Multi-statement JSX handlers must be named functions — not inline closures with 2+ statements.
4. UI strings via next-intl message keys — no hardcoded user-facing copy.
5. Respect file length limits; split before you grow past them.

## Check catalog (what each script enforces)

| Check | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| **secrets** | No hardcoded API keys, tokens, passwords. |
| **hardcoded-text** | No raw UI strings; use `messages/*.json` + next-intl. |
| **locale-sync** | Locale JSON keys stay synchronized across languages. |
| **arch-rules** | No raw `process.env` outside config; no inline `style={}`; no `as any`; RTL-safe classes (`ms`/`me`/`ps`/`pe`/`inset-s`/`inset-e`, not `ml`/`mr`); no hex colors (theme tokens); no generic `throw new Error()` — use domain/`AppError`. |
| **tailwind-classes** | No deprecated Tailwind positioning: use `inset-s-*` / `inset-e-*` instead of `start-*` / `end-*`. Keep `ms-/me-/ps-/pe-` and `text-start`/`text-end`. |
| **structure** | Only allowed `src/` top-level dirs and root files. |
| **metadata** | Every `page.tsx` is a server component with SEO `metadata` / `openGraph`. |
| **types** | Ban `any`, `!`, `@ts-ignore`, `as unknown`, bare `Function` / `Object`. |
| **nest-type** | Ban inline/nested object type literals in params/props/generics — export named types from `src/types/`. |
| **api-urls** | No hardcoded `http(s)://` outside approved config. |
| **comments** | Zero comments in `src/`. |
| **console** | No leftover `console.log` in app code. |
| **feature-boundaries** | Keep feature isolation; share via `components/`, `lib/`, `types/`. |
| **banned-deps** | No axios / react-hook-form / moment / dayjs / lodash / bcrypt on the client. Use project fetch client + approved form/date libs. |
| **tenancy** | Storefront must respect shop/slug tenancy; no cross-shop leakage. |
| **financial-safety** | Display money via shared formatters; no ad-hoc float money math. |
| **error-boundaries** | Keep required route error boundaries. |
| **catch-handling** | Meaningful catch handling — no empty catches. |
| **max-lines** | Pages ≤ 100; layouts ≤ 300; hooks ≤ 300; API/schemas ≤ 350; components ≤ 480; default ≤ 400. |
| **storage-safety** | Safe browser storage only. |
| **button-safety** | Explicit `type="button"` / `type="submit"` on buttons in forms. |
| **accessibility** | Semantic HTML / accessible labels and navigation. |
| **react-purity** | No side effects during render. |
| **nextjs-features** | App Router best practices enforced by the auditor. |
| **mutation-hooks** | Mutations follow project patterns. |
| **clean-handlers** | Named handlers for multi-statement JSX events. |
| **list-tables** | List UIs use the approved responsive table patterns when applicable. |
| **unused** / **orphans** / **knip** | No dead code, unused imports, or orphan modules. |
| **duplicates** / **duplicate-audit** | Avoid copy-paste clones. |
| **lint** / **typecheck** / **test** / **build** | Must pass. |

## Types pattern

```ts
// ❌
function Card(props: { title: string; href: string }) {}

// ✅
import type { StoreCardProps } from '@/types/store'
function Card(props: StoreCardProps) {}
```

## Handlers pattern

```tsx
// ❌
onClick={() => { track(); router.push(href) }}

// ✅
const handleClick = () => {
  track()
  router.push(href)
}
<button type="button" onClick={handleClick} />
```

## Storefront notes

- Prefer server components by default; mark `'use client'` only when needed.
- Images/logos follow existing media helpers and placeholders.
- Keep RTL-safe Tailwind (logical properties) for ur/ps locales.
